  "body": "**Research note (no \u03ba claim).** For the [#2322](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2322) T74 words (base of the open #2349 / #2363 / #2374 line), this certifies the remaining owner-fill headroom and gives exact prices for local inventory moves.\n\n| finding (LP-ceiling differences on the #2322 words, both providers, at a = #2374's \u03ba) | value |\n|---|---|\n| **certified cap, any legal whole-helper owner fill of the #2322 words** | **b < 0.001697195759** |\n| headroom above #2374's claim (0.0016971949509) | \u2264 8.1e-10 |\n| one more #2322-type handoff (same reshapes) | +4.27e-8 each, linear up to 12 (+5.13e-7) |\n| one #2339-type low alias | \u22121.91e-7 |\n| one #2339-type high alias | exactly 0 |\n| one (1,1)\u2192(2) merge of two rank-1 climbs (no width change) | **+1.13e-7** |\n| the 26 such target merges that come with #2339's low aliases, on their own | **+2.94e-6** |\n\n**Why.** A climb of d dimensions pays one child of rank d, and total rank mass is fixed. So a move changes b only through the *shape* of the paid children, plus the helper widths acting through the width-aware bin patterns of #2387 / #2360.\n- **Cap.** It comes from the #2387 LP with an exact rational dual and 800-bit enclosures (W\u00b7mu margin 1.85e-7, zero dual repair). The certificate does not reject #2374's claimed point. Owner relocations on these words therefore have at most 8.1e-10 left.\n- **#2312 \u2192 #2322 decomposes exactly** into four handoffs:\n  - remove (1,1,1,1) helpers 619/621/622/623;\n  - X lenders 1/4/6/12 go (5,1,1,1)\u2192(2,1,1,1,1,1,1);\n  - partners 616/617/618/620 go (4,1,1,1,1)\u2192(3,2,1,1,1).\n\n  The LP predicts a +1.96e-7 ceiling gain; the realized claims gained +1.69e-7.\n- **#2269 \u2192 #2339 decomposes exactly.**\n  - A low alias's lender takes over the helper's climb, a net \u2212h(3) locally, but the width change costs more through the bins.\n  - A high alias is exactly neutral.\n  - The 26 changed targets each gain exactly one (1,1)\u2192(2) merge. These merges alone would be worth +2.94e-6, which dwarfs the owner-fill race.\n\n**Leads (priced, not constructed).**\n- 33 helpers still climb (1,1,1,1): the 32 #2226 low lenders plus 653.\n- 12 X registers still climb (5,1,1,1) and lend no warp: 31 33 49 55 68 74 80 83 85 88 98 101.\n- **Block 53** has exactly #2322's pre-handoff pattern: 653 next to four (4,1,1,1,1) partners 648/649/650/652. #2374 notes that alias 653 was dropped.\n\nWhether any of these admits a legal coherent handoff is **not checked here**; it is listed under open next questions.\n\n**Checks.**\n- `move_prices.py` recounts which register pays each child in 8 pinned words. Each recount equals the word's reported profile and width inventory, and the decompositions add up exactly. Controls cover move signs, high-alias neutrality, the mass identity, and the certificate not rejecting #2374.\n- `independent_recount.py` was written by a separate AI reviewer subagent from a plain statement of the frame rules, with its own GF(2) code and no shared code. It reproduces the profiles, the change set and the site lists for both providers.\n- Package metadata (`--check-only`) passes; 65/65 research tests pass (2 skipped); 3.10 grammar check passes.\n- Everything was run on CPython 3.14.4. The registered 3.12 replay was not run locally.\n\n**Reproduce** (standard library only; `--fetch` pulls `refs/pull/{2312,2322,2269,2339}/head` if commits fb76f799 / 002304ef / b479fc55 / bf1742ae are absent; every word file is blob- and sha256-pinned):\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2322-move-prices/move_prices.py --fetch   # ~16 s -> PASS_T74_MOVE_PRICES cap=0.001697195759 handoff_db=+4.272e-08 low_alias_db=-1.906e-07 high_alias_net=0 sites=33/12\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2322-move-prices/independent_recount.py   # -> PASS_T74_INDEPENDENT_RECOUNT\n```\n`vendor/pr2387/` holds pinned byte copies of #2387's `ceiling_lp.py` and `fill_check80.py` (this author). `move_prices.py` patches one line of `local_recount` at load time, to record the register that pays each child.\n\n**Scope.** This is a pricing screen on fixed pinned words. Windows, families and ports are dropped, so prices are ceiling differences, not realized gains. The cap is a relaxation ceiling for unsplit helpers on the unchanged #2269 bin stock. No handoff or merge is constructed, and the selected frontier is untouched. Base: canonical main `0fdd7d82`. Task card: `complex-new-helper-inventory`, scope refined.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2322 Vlado Vojdanovski.\n- #2312 / #2269 Jeremy Kothe.\n- #2374 / #2349 jeremykothe2 and #2363 mason-hale.\n- #2226 Cinna Davis.\n- #2360 Jeremy Diviney and #1129 Ali Romman (pattern dual).\n- #2394 commdata2338 (native anticipatory prefix).\n- #1995 / #2013 (fixed-word frame bounds).\n- #1319 / #1297 T74 lineage.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
